WEBVTT

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:07.540
Back then, I swore I would live together with Maia.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.770
Despite that... Why?!

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:13.730
Join.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.630
Why?

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.440
Why?

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:51.810
Why can't I win?

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:58.890
At one time, man was one with the world of truth.

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:04.290
But the written word brought forth prosperity and suffering.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:19.510
<i>The kanji for "love" and "grief " look very similar</i>

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:24.910
<i>When I realized that, dawn suddenly broke</i>

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:30.690
<i>The air was filled with so much</i> <i>silence that "blue" "fought"</i>

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:37.030
<i>When suddenly you slid in to the right of me</i>

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.930
<i>Rippling with a clatter</i>

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:42.870
<i>and tangled in red thread</i>

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:47.770
<i>and a 39-degree fever of passion</i>

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:53.210
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:59.280
<i>A crown worn on high with pride</i>

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:04.720
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>"soothe" my hidden "heart below"</i>

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:10.730
<i>Its form is too much to handle right now</i>

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:13.660
<i>God's wisdom, the "h" in "her"</i>

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:16.400
<i>With a tearful, feverish gaze</i>

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:19.340
<i>let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon</i>

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:22.170
<i>(Let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon)</i>

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:29.580
<i>The things you can do are so striking</i>

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:37.820
"A Great Victory! Our Savior"

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:47.830
I hate this... It's just too painful...

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:50.730
If living brings me this much pain--

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:53.340
if this is fate--

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:57.070
I hope this whole world disappears.

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:11.750
What's wrong?

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.060
It's coming.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:14.860
Is this...?

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.960
It's a new M.J.B.K. reading.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.590
What?

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:24.400
The great word which changed its form in response to Subete's spirit

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:28.270
is now regaining its original shape.

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:34.910
"Nothingness." So this is the great word, huh?

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:39.110
Though I'm surprised a word turned into an M.J.B.K. without an ampule.

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:41.710
Is this Subete's power, too?

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:48.890
What is it that binds your heart?

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:52.630
A dream? Or is it her?

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:57.600
Yet another person vanishes, dragged off by someone who's already gone...

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:02.330
As the one left behind, there's nothing more dissatisfying.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.790
This place... We've been here before.

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:20.520
The world from which all words originate--the Logos World.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.760
Is that an M.J.B.K.?

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:31.700
Has it finally taken form?

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:35.500
Master Sougon!

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:41.270
The nothingness M.J.B.K. which will erase every concept from this world.

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:47.140
Akira, I have a favor to ask.

00:04:56.860 --> 00:05:01.800
Master Sougon, I want to talk with you once more.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:07.470
You once said people, having been ensnared by the world of words,

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.810
were in the midst of misfortune.

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:14.340
It's true, people can be swayed greatly by words and their concepts.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.840
Ours is a brittle and weak existence.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:25.820
But for me... I can't see that weakness as wrong.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.730
Because they have something precious to them,

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:32.930
a single word can sadden or hurt them.

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:36.070
But conversely, it can also make them laugh.

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:38.360
Yes, so...

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:50.010
...people aren't misfortunate!

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:56.540
Maia... You've grown in the short time we've been apart.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:00.460
Master Sougon!

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:06.230
Poisoned by a world of folly, you grew into a person who must be erased.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:09.900
You understand nothing.

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:14.300
Nothing of the proper relationship between people and words.

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:15.940
Relationship?

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:20.980
At one time, in order to leave their mark for future generations,

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:25.410
and to record the feelings they could not leave unconveyed,

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:27.550
people created writing.

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:34.460
What lay behind this were strong wishes that they had to communicate.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:38.630
But what of modern society?

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:40.900
Their overdeveloped culture

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:45.170
has created internet culture where superficial, meaningless words abound.

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:45.170
"Takayuki: Want to go out?"

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:45.170
"Ani: lol no way"

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:47.740
They communicate with words that have lost all meaning.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:53.010
People even feel a sense of security in these fake relationships.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.670
"Recipient: Chief Gotou

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.670
Title: About the Golf Convention

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.670
Chief Gotou, Thank you for your

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.670
invitation today!! Playing golf was fun.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.670
Please, let me join you again sometime."

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:52.170
"Mayorin: I had a lot of fun! Eating with you

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:52.170
is the best, Kou! Let's do it again sometime.

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:52.170
Kou: I like you too, Mayorin!"

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:55.140
"Recipient: Chief Nakamori

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:55.140
Title: Corrections for the Pamphlet

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:55.140
We strive to balance environmental protections

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:55.140
and the conveniences of society."

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:55.140
What folly!

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:59.350
The all-too-convenient tool of writing has taken on a life of its own,

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:02.420
and that is what has led to this misfortune.

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:08.020
If writing makes the relations between people superficial, it must be destroyed.

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:11.930
So people can truly be connected.

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:16.830
If we lose writing, many people now living will be hurt by that.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:19.770
You know that when you say all this.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:23.170
There is nothing more for us to discuss.

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:25.710
Master Sougon...

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:30.110
No, Sougon! You are wrong!

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:33.620
If you won't understand, no matter how I shout...

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:36.210
...then I will stop you!

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:39.690
That is not possible.

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:44.030
I was surprised when you called me to pick you up at the TV station.

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:45.890
You don't have any work today, do you?

00:07:45.890 --> 00:07:47.560
What were you doing here?

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:52.840
Well, they wanted to touch base about the upcoming shoot.

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:55.840
Still, you should have called. I was worried.

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:57.860
Yeah, I'm sorry.

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:01.670
"Tree" "Building"

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:07.010
"Building"

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:09.990
H-Huh?

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:11.550
What is this?

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:12.210
"Board"

00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:18.990
"Board"

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:21.700
Did something happen?

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:26.700
I feel like there was something here up until now...

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:31.410
How did I input commands again?

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:33.440
A concept has vanished!

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:38.880
If a word vanishes from the
Logos World, its concept is lost.

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:36.210
"Stairs"

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:43.890
That means its existence is erased from people's consciousness.

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:44.790
"Building"

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:51.260
If people can't perceive it, they can't see or touch it.

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:46.860
"Stairs"

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:50.030
"Stairs"

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:54.200
If we continue to lose words,

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:57.470
we will lose the ability to perceive anything

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:01.540
and be left behind in a void.

00:08:58.530 --> 00:08:59.940
"Wheel"

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:05.940
And, when they finally lose the ability to perceive themselves,

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:08.910
people will cease to be people.

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:11.940
That will be the end of civilization.

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:18.790
Sougon... Kenzaki!

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:20.480
"Fun"

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.130
"Fun"

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:29.730
"Building"

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:32.830
"Theater"

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:37.400
"Theater"

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:43.150
No... N-No more...!

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:45.340
"Mother"

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:51.090
"Mother"

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:53.820
No!

00:09:57.960 --> 00:09:59.660
Stop it!

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:05.420
Mu!

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:14.670
Farewell, human world.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:31.290
Mu! Mu! Mu, Mu! Mu! Mu...

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:34.700
Subete's name means "everything" and represents all existence.

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:38.500
Was his everything swallowed up, leaving him with nothingness?

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:40.300
How pathetic.

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:44.010
Once words and concepts have been extinguished from the world,

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:48.880
you will become the key, if you are qualified to, at least.

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:52.540
You still struggle?

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:56.050
"The World"

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:01.390
I won't... let you take it...

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:03.060
Why do you struggle?

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:07.930
There is already practically nothing left in the world.

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:12.400
It's no good... Though she was with me until just a moment ago...

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:16.340
She's gone... Gone...

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:17.670
Don't give up!

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:19.940
Big Brother Hayato!

00:11:19.940 --> 00:11:23.380
Akira has the world in his grasp now.

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:27.280
He's fighting desperately to save it from being stolen away!

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:29.520
I could understand that.

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:32.550
Because becoming a politician and leading the world in the right direction...

00:11:32.550 --> 00:11:34.610
That is my dream.

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:41.630
Even if I lose everything, so long as the world itself remains,

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:44.200
I cannot give up!

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:46.300
It must be the same for all of you!

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:48.740
Milkman... You...

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:51.370
Our dreams... The things we treasure...

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:55.210
So long as the world is there, we'll have many chances to get them back.

00:11:55.210 --> 00:11:58.080
I won't let go!

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:00.280
For I am...

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:03.550
We should all have it in our hands.

00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:05.650
The same shine that he has!

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:06.620
"Savior"

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:09.590
Mu!

00:12:09.590 --> 00:12:11.760
It won't end!

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:13.460
For I am...

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:15.760
Yes, remember!

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:17.770
Even if people have lost it,

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:20.770
"Savior"

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:20.770
there is something we still have!

00:12:20.770 --> 00:12:22.500
I am...

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:25.140
You're right.

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:30.510
In our hands, we have this word, which will never stop shining!

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:31.780
"Savior"

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:32.680
And to convey this word...

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:34.580
...we have voices!

00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:44.430
Kokone!

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:45.920
Everyone!

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:52.930
This is farewell, you people who are tied down by words.

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:54.470
What is so funny?

00:12:54.470 --> 00:12:58.310
I know, Akira. I could hear their voices, as well!

00:12:58.310 --> 00:13:03.180
What will save this world... won't be my voice alone!

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:07.980
The true heroes appear, eh?

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:10.510
Sousei Gattai! Dash!

00:13:16.660 --> 00:13:18.150
Jin!

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:24.700
Akira! Maia!

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:26.670
Yeah, let's do it!

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:28.300
Shine!

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:32.740
Angel!

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:36.080
G-Give it back! My love!

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:37.910
Mu, mu, mu!

00:13:36.910 --> 00:13:37.910
"Love"

00:13:37.910 --> 00:13:40.210
Moonlight Cannon!

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:43.690
I'm still ready to go!

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:45.310
Bloom beautifully!

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:49.980
Rin!

00:13:52.590 --> 00:13:57.500
<i>Un, deux, trois</i>!
<i>Un, deux, trois</i>! <i>Un</i>! <i>Deux</i>! <i>Trois</i>!

00:13:57.500 --> 00:13:58.500
Reach them!

00:13:58.500 --> 00:13:59.990
Fly!

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:04.700
Sei!

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:09.540
Gai!

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:12.110
Break through the sound barrier!

00:14:12.110 --> 00:14:14.240
Wings of Calm Wind!

00:14:20.220 --> 00:14:21.220
Dance!

00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:22.850
Pierce!

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:28.190
Zai!

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:32.460
Ryu!

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:34.130
"Flame"

00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:38.270
Heat Haze Dance!

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:42.440
Break through!

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:49.240
Absurd!

00:14:50.590 --> 00:14:52.820
Shout!

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:54.310
Kou!

00:14:56.590 --> 00:14:57.560
"Fist"

00:14:58.060 --> 00:15:00.160
Nothingness is an absence of anything.

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:04.730
But at the same time, it is limitless!

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:07.670
Mu...

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:09.660
Mugen Punch!

00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:18.140
There is no limit to possibility!

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:26.450
Mu!

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:28.450
Roar!

00:15:32.190 --> 00:15:33.960
Phoenix!

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:39.760
The Blood of a Passionate Man!

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:48.210
Transcending the infinite, it shines down from heaven.

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:47.810
"Heaven"

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:50.550
This light which leaps through the sky.

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:50.180
"Sky"

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:52.380
Soar towards eternity!

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:51.980
"Eternity"

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:54.480
Like the dragon!

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:52.880
"Insect"

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:53.850
"Dragon"

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:56.220
Reverberating here is the king's...

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:55.780
"King"

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:58.880
...sound! Our name is...

00:15:56.320 --> 00:15:58.650
"Sound"

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:02.890
...Aquarion!

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:02.360
"Aquarion"

00:16:02.890 --> 00:16:06.900
For as long as our voices last, we will not let things end!

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:08.530
For I am...

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:10.170
We are...

00:16:10.170 --> 00:16:11.700
We all are...

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:14.830
...the saviors!

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:23.040
Muuu...!

00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:39.230
Maia!

00:16:39.230 --> 00:16:40.430
Subete...

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:42.000
Where are Akira and Maia?

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:44.000
Why haven't they come back?

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:48.400
Did the force-return program not activate for them?

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:53.040
Maia... Finally, I'm able to see you...

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:55.410
Subete, you're...

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:59.380
Come back to me, Maia. For me...

00:16:59.380 --> 00:17:02.180
...you're absolutely essential.

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:06.240
Maia?

00:17:07.890 --> 00:17:10.960
Sougon Kenzaki! A threat to the world!

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:12.860
Verbalize.

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:14.350
Nothingness!

00:17:17.630 --> 00:17:19.230
Verbalize.

00:17:23.470 --> 00:17:27.880
One with Verbalism Ability as advanced as yours must understand.

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:29.710
The folly of humans

00:17:29.710 --> 00:17:33.750
is dependent on words and connected by superficial discourse.

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:35.920
For as long as the written word exists,

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:39.390
there can be no true connections between people.

00:17:39.390 --> 00:17:40.720
I can't hear it.

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:45.590
From your voice, I don't hear the sound of one who's been connected to others.

00:17:45.590 --> 00:17:51.120
You're just blaming words for your weakness and inability to connect.

00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:55.640
You must have been lonely all this time.

00:17:55.640 --> 00:17:59.840
Don't think everyone in this world is the same as you.

00:17:59.840 --> 00:18:01.810
In this world, feelings have been communicated by writing

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:05.250
and bonds formed that way, I'm sure of it.

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:11.080
For that which chooses our path is always our own two feet.

00:18:07.150 --> 00:18:08.920
"Foot"

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:31.470
The "nothingness" kanji originates

00:18:31.470 --> 00:18:35.010
from a pictograph which depicted people dancing.

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:38.310
By walking forward on their own feet, can people...

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:46.890
...dance through the air, even in a world of nothingness?

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:49.490
--Akira!
--Dad... Dad!

00:18:49.490 --> 00:18:50.980
Maia!

00:18:59.730 --> 00:19:02.570
Dad... Where are you? Dad!

00:19:09.180 --> 00:19:14.250
Akira Kaibuki... I was supposed to be the chosen one.

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:19.590
So, why is it? Why do you keep taking everything away from me?

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:23.590
My father... And Maia...

00:19:23.590 --> 00:19:26.260
What the hell are you?!

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:29.700
I'm just... a savior.

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:34.170
Don't give me that bullshit!

00:19:34.170 --> 00:19:37.910
Give back my precious Maia!

00:19:37.910 --> 00:19:40.940
That's not right, Subete.

00:19:40.940 --> 00:19:45.380
From the very beginning, you were never really looking at me.

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:48.010
What you were seeing the whole time was...

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:53.050
...that we were similar people.

00:19:53.050 --> 00:19:59.190
You longed for me as a replacement for your image in the mirror.

00:19:59.190 --> 00:20:01.530
No, I...

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:04.030
You've changed.

00:20:04.030 --> 00:20:09.800
The Subete who saved me that moonlit night is gone now...

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:20.780
This is unnecessary.

00:20:20.780 --> 00:20:25.120
Don't think that living alone will bring any salvation.

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:29.490
Dad!

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:30.490
Let's go.

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:31.830
B-But...!

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:33.260
--Dad!
--Akira!

00:20:33.260 --> 00:20:34.260
Dad!

00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:36.930
I see... I remember now.

00:20:36.930 --> 00:20:39.420
Master Sougon! Subete!

00:20:40.240 --> 00:20:43.500
No! Master Sougon!

00:20:46.170 --> 00:20:47.640
"Sun"

00:20:58.120 --> 00:21:02.420
Huh? I seem to recall being in pitch darkness...

00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:06.760
Defeating the M.J.B.K. restored the lost concepts.

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:09.000
Does that mean we won?

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:10.490
Karan...

00:21:14.770 --> 00:21:16.700
You guys are all right?

00:21:16.700 --> 00:21:18.540
What about Akira and Maia?

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:20.170
Iwagami, bring them up on screen.

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:21.800
R-Right!

00:21:26.810 --> 00:21:28.850
Look!

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:30.290
All right!

00:21:30.290 --> 00:21:32.550
Yeah!

00:21:32.550 --> 00:21:34.220
Thank goodness.

00:21:37.530 --> 00:21:39.490
We were able to finish it...

00:21:39.490 --> 00:21:43.030
...without playing our forbidden trump card.

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:44.530
What's wrong?

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:47.000
"Voice ID

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:47.000
Maia Tsukigane"

00:21:45.800 --> 00:21:47.840
I●●●

00:21:47.840 --> 00:21:50.370
I'll hear you out for as long as you want later.

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:53.210
But there's only one thing we should be saying now.

00:21:53.210 --> 00:21:54.900
One thing...?

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:01.380
One, two...

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:03.820
Welcome back!

00:22:06.890 --> 00:22:10.090
--We're back.
--Y-You're the one who's saying it?!

00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:19.760
Welcome, legend.

00:22:36.420 --> 00:22:39.890
<i>Je-Je t'aime communication</i>

00:22:39.890 --> 00:22:49.890
<i>Oh, you aren't making a bit of</i> <i>eye contact with me while you talk</i>

00:22:49.930 --> 00:22:59.140
<i>Are you texting some far-off</i> <i>neighboring world or something?</i>

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:04.270
<i>Because this isn't communication at all</i>

00:23:06.210 --> 00:23:12.750
<i>You'd at least understand that much</i>

00:23:12.750 --> 00:23:18.760
<i>even if the times suddenly changed, right?</i>

00:23:18.760 --> 00:23:22.760
<i>Give me je t'aime communication sometimes</i>

00:23:22.760 --> 00:23:26.170
<i>Look at me, answer me, and tell me</i>

00:23:26.170 --> 00:23:32.670
<i>I mean, this is practically</i> <i>like talking to a computer</i>

00:23:32.670 --> 00:23:35.680
<i>A-Adieu application</i>

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:42.320
<i>Even if it means staying lonely</i> <i>in my heart, if it'll connect us</i>

00:23:42.320 --> 00:23:48.690
<i>then, please, at least show</i> <i>your smile to me alone</i>

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:52.990
You haven't drunk any milk lately, huh, Milkman?

00:23:52.990 --> 00:23:54.430
Stop calling me that!

00:23:54.430 --> 00:23:57.170
Milk is highly nutritious.
You should drink some, Milkman.

00:23:57.170 --> 00:23:58.630
Kaibuki, not you, too...

00:23:58.630 --> 00:24:00.000
Nice one, Saviorman!

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.000
Your humor has a new layer of polish now that the fighting's done, huh?

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:03.600
Next time: Episode 14.

00:24:02.470 --> 00:24:05.140
"Episode 14: Show It! You at Your Worst"

00:24:03.600 --> 00:24:05.140
"Show It! You at Your Worst."

00:24:05.140 --> 00:24:07.440
It's gonna keep going just a little longer!

00:24:07.440 --> 00:24:08.540
It's going to continue for quite a while.

00:24:08.540 --> 00:24:09.810
What will?
